 a first generation K-pop idol dance group which disbanded in 2000 but reunited in 2016. Unlike most of the other members, Ko left the entertainment industry and started his own company. He made his first television appearance in years when he appeared at Sechs Kies' reunion special on Infinite Challenge. Due to his family and work commitments he did not sign a contract with the group's new label YG Entertainment or promote with them as a performer but was considered to be part of the group until 2018. From January 2017 to May 2019, he and his son appeared on the reality show The Return of Superman.","title":"Ko Ji-yong","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ko_Ji-yong"}},"Q12598115":{"id":"Q12598115","name":"Basick","ko":"베이식","birthName":"이철주","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Cheol-joo"],"birth":"1986-08-12","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["MC","rapper","singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[{"name":"Rainbow Bridge World","korean":true,"id":"Q16174772","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/realbasick/","x":"https://x.com/basickk_","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/4aeb4915-b7de-4b12-a601-063176996ee6"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/%EB%B2%A0%EC%9D%B4%EC%8B%9D_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EB%B2%A0%EC%9D%B4%EC%8B%9D_(cropped).jpg","author":"Pabian","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Lee Cheol-joo, better known by his stage name Basick (베이식), is a South Korean rapper under OUTLIVE. He won the fourth season of Mnet's rap competition Show Me the Money.","title":"Basick","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basick"}},"Q12613091":{"id":"Q12613091","name":"Lee Hae-in","ko":"임이지","birthName":"이지영","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Leezy","Im Leezy","Lee Ji-young"],"birth":"1986-04-19","death":"","birthplace"